<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Octavius Mamilius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 496 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Octavius Mamilius was the leader of Tusculum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latium">Latium</a> and son-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus">Tarquinius Superbus</a>, the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. According to Roman tradition, after the Tarquins were expelled he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> League against Rome and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-regillus">Battle of Lake Regillus</a> around 496 BCE, after which Tusculum became one of Rome's closest allies.</p></div>
